      <h2>Step-by-Step Salary Calculation Workflow</h2>
      <p>
        A frequent misconception is assuming that a 2.86x fitment factor will double or triple your net monthly take-home salary overnight. That is not how pay commission implementation works. Because accumulated Dearness Allowance is rolled into the base salary, the DA rate resets to 0% upon rollout. 
      </p>
      <p>The standard arithmetic proceeds through six stages:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Step 1 (Base Recalibration):</strong> Multiply current 7th CPC Basic Pay by the fitment factor (e.g., ₹35,400 × 2.86 = ₹1,01,244).</li>
        <li><strong>Step 2 (DA Reset):</strong> Dearness Allowance resets to 0% initially, gradually compounding again every six months according to future AICPI-IW index numbers.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 3 (HRA Revision):</strong> Recompute House Rent Allowance on the enlarged base pay (30% for Class X, 20% for Class Y, and 10% for Class Z cities).</li>
        <li><strong>Step 4 (Transport Allowance):</strong> Apply baseline city-level Transport Allowance rates without immediate DA inflation loading.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 5 (Statutory Deductions):</strong> Recalculate mandatory pension deductions (10% of Basic Pay under NPS/UPS frameworks) plus revised CGHS healthcare slabs and professional taxes.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 6 (Net Pay Determination):</strong> Subtract total statutory deductions from the new gross figure to find actual in-hand take-home pay.</li>
      </ul>

